      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In spite of the continuous growth of myocardial revascularisation techniques, stable angina remains an important clinical burden. In France, and based upon estimates from the European Society of Cardiology and from diverse epidemiological sources, 2 million people are likely to have stable angina. Though primary and secondary prevention are improving, this figure is likely to increase further, in particular because of the constant aging of the population (20% of patients more than 80 years of age have angina), but also because of the epidemics proportions that diabetes mellitus and obesity take."},
